  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "feat(pool): introduce zero-allocation LockObject<T> with RAII scope and benchmarks\n\n      - Add `LockObject<T>` inheriting from `PooledObject<T>` for thread-safe value wrapping.\n      - Leverage .NET 9 `System.Threading.Lock` with aggressive inlining for minimal lock contention overhead.\n      - Provide `Scope` ref-struct pattern to guarantee deterministic, allocation-free RAII lock acquisition.\n      - Benchmark results verify 0 bytes allocated with pure uncontended synchronization cost (~13-14ns delta).",
